  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "The leaves of this cultivar are deeply divided into seven lobes which are narrow, elongate-lanceolate, and taper to a long, slender point. Leaf size is about 4-5 cm long and 5-6 cm wide. The lobes separate almost to the leaf base and radiate sharply outward. The edges of each lobe are slightly curved up or trough shaped and prominently double serrated. The reddish petioles are 2-3 cm long. The basic leaf color is light green. Margins of new leaves are tinted with a bright brick red. In the fall, yellow to crimson blends appear. This medium-strong grower forms an upright plant up to 5 m tall. It is quite vigorous and hardy. One Japanese writer described the leaf shape as \"like a crystal of snow\" and unique. The little-known 'Mure hibari', which means \"flock of skylarks,\" is indeed a beautiful cultivar."
  },
